It is easily tested, I just tried in wizmode with the arrow traps that
started the thread, and you are wrong about something; none of the
stacks merged after dropping/picking up, and when I identified them
they were all different in at least one of
Blessed/Cursed/Uncursed("BUC") status, enchantment, or poison status.

You're probably misremembering something--I certainly haven't seen
other people reporting anything like that on this list.

My best guess is that you're not accounting for differences in
identification level.

Say you are carrying:
a - 3 uncursed daggers
(which you've already BUC identified on an altar) and then you pick
up:
b - 2 daggers

Since they are of unknown BUC status, they don't stack.

Then, later, you go to an altar, drop everything, and pick it back up
and you have only:
a - 5 uncursed daggers

This is not a bug.  When you first had 2 stacks, one was of _known_
uncursed daggers, the other was of daggers in an unknown BUC state and
the code intentionally won't let you identify their BUC state by
stacking them with a.

What _might_ be a bug is that when you identify the second stack, it
doesn't automatically merge the two at that time.

Stacking other identified info works the same way; if you have "a - a
blessed +0 dagger; b - a blessed dagger" they won't stack even if b is
also +0.  Later on you read a ?identify and get b identified; then if
you drop b and pick it back up it will stack.



